+---
+id: dl-003-createpatch-array-diff-trim-common-prefix-suffix-no-lcs
+type: decision-log
+title: "createPatch array diff: trim common prefix/suffix, no LCS"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+`createPatch` must emit only what changed. Arrays have no keys, so a naive index-wise diff rewrites every element after an insertion or removal.
+
+## Decision
+
+Objects are diffed member by member (removes, then recursion/adds, in key insertion order, so output is deterministic). Arrays skip the common leading and trailing elements, diff the remaining overlap index-wise, then remove or append the surplus. No LCS, no `move`/`copy` operations.
+
+## Consequences
+
+A single insertion, removal or edit in an array gives one small operation. Scattered multi-element changes in one array may yield more operations than a minimal LCS diff, but the patch stays correct, small in practice and cheap to compute (linear).
+
